Have you used the castle wand yet?  The glaring upgrade you can make
is to #twoweapon; it's a _massive_ damage boost.  The glaring safety
net you can put into place is a "oLifeSaving.  For the former, you
need an alternate source of reflection--that means SDSM, which means
you need MR (CoMR).  Before wishing any of that up, check the dragons
in the back of the castle for silver scales, and the armory for the
cloak.

"oLS is nice for a first-timer as it allows you to avoid permanent
death from something just because you're unfamiliar with it.

Also note that magic markers are a _great_ wish--they can get you AC,
HP, XL, enchant weapon, genocide, free teleports, mapping, all kinds
of stuff.  Beyond that, teleport control, levitation, and conflict are
the big needs if you lack them.

Excalibur's the 2nd best offensive melee weapon in the game IMO, after
Grayswandir, so that's more than adequate (things like Frostbrand/
Firebrand/Mjollnir/Sceptre are just too limited in what they affect,
and other than the Sceptre the destroy inventory).  Once you get
replacement reflection/MR, #twoweapon it and the saber.



